From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add the Gateway GWTN133-1

Add the Gateway GWTN133-1, a 13.3" Snapdragon 850 clamshell that
Huawei built on the MateBook E 2019's board. Its ACPI tables carry
Huawei's OEM ID and the MateBook's subsystem IDs (CLS00850, 19E53E0E),
and its DSDT differs from the MateBook's in four places, so the tree
includes the MateBook's and changes only those.

- The panel is a Sharp LQ133M1JW15-E at 1920x1080 (EDID SHP 0x1447)
  behind the same SN65DSI86 bridge, so it is a generic edp-panel,
  which reads its mode from the EDID. panel-edp doesn't list it yet and
  falls back to conservative delays.
- The keyboard is a HID device on the embedded controller (QTEC0001)
  at 0x3a on i2c0 (QUP0 SE0), interrupt GPIO 52, descriptor at 0x1.
- The touchpad (HTIX5288) is at 0x2c on i2c3, interrupt GPIO 3, and
  its _DSM puts the HID descriptor at 0x20.
- There is no touchscreen and no fingerprint reader, so i2c5 is off.

GPIO 0, 1 and 3 belong to the keyboard bus and the touchpad here, and
Windows drives them from the OS, so only GPIO 2 and the 81 to 84 SPI
block stay reserved. The tablet mode switch goes, since the laptop has
no tablet mode and nothing in its tables uses GPIO 79.

Jingzhou Zhu adapted his MateBook tree for this laptop in 2023 and
found the same differences. His tree puts the touchpad descriptor at
0x1 and keeps GPIO 0 to 3 reserved, which stops i2c0 from muxing.

The "gateway" vendor prefix is Gateway Communications, a telecom
maker, so the compatible uses Acer's, which owns the Gateway brand.

The firmware paths stay the MateBook's. Its images are signed under
Qualcomm's QCT Root CA 1 for OEM ID 0x0015, model 0x0001, and the
MateBook's Windows driver binds to this laptop's subsystem IDs. Not
booted on the laptop yet.

Link: https://github.com/aarch64-laptops/build/issues/84#issuecomment-1746527461
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 .../dts/qcom/sdm850-gateway-gwtn133-1.dts     | 87 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 87 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-gateway-gwtn133-1.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-gateway-gwtn133-1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-gateway-gwtn133-1.dts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..95790e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm850-gateway-gwtn133-1.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,87 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
+/*
+ * Gateway GWTN133-1
+ *
+ * Huawei's MateBook E 2019 board as a clamshell. Its DSDT is the
+ * MateBook's with a Sharp LQ133M1JW15-E 1920x1080 panel behind the same
+ * SN65DSI86 bridge, the keyboard on i2c0 and the touchpad on i2c3, and
+ * neither the touchscreen nor the fingerprint reader.
+ */
+
+#include "sdm850-huawei-matebook-e-2019.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "Gateway GWTN133-1";
+	compatible = "acer,gateway-gwtn133-1", "qcom,sdm845";
+	chassis-type = "laptop";
+
+	gpio-keys {
+		pinctrl-0 = <&volume_up_gpio>;
+
+		/delete-node/ switch-mode;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c0 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	keyboard@3a {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x3a>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x1>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 52 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&kb_int_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c3 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	status = "okay";
+
+	touchpad@2c {
+		compatible = "hid-over-i2c";
+		reg = <0x2c>;
+		hid-descr-addr = <0x20>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 3 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&tpad_int_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		wakeup-source;
+	};
+};
+
+&i2c5 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&panel {
+	compatible = "edp-panel";
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	gpio-reserved-ranges = <2 1>, <81 4>;
+
+	kb_int_default: kb-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio52";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	tpad_int_default: tpad-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio3";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+};
-- 
